From: U2W build
Subject: [PATCH] aacdec: keep the output-buffer check; an input byte count passed as size means "unknown"

0.1.5 added
  if (timeDataSize_extern < numChannels*frameSize) ErrorStatus = AAC_DEC_OUTPUT_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL;
0.1.4, the vendor library AppleCarPlay was built against (byte-identical in every Carlinkit
firmware 2023-2025), ignored timeDataSize and decoded the frame in place.

Measured in the car (2026-10-19, VW MIB2G, instrumented build): on its AAC-ELD call-audio path
(AOT 39, 16 kHz, mono, frame 480) AppleCarPlay passes as timeDataSize the input byte count it
just handed to aacDecoder_Fill (2, 25, 45, 74, 117, 148..181: the packet lengths).  0.1.6
rejected every frame with 0x200c and calls were silent in the car.  The CarPlay SDK's AAC-ELD
converter only decodes into a buffer of at least kAudioSamplesPerPacket_AAC_ELD (480) frames.

aacDecoder_Fill records the input byte count per decoder handle.  When timeDataSize equals it,
the caller passed its input length, not an output size: write the frame as 0.1.4 did
(numChannels*frameSize samples, the vendor footprint) and log it once per handle.  Every other
value keeps the 0.1.6 check, so a real undersized buffer is still rejected.

--- a/libAACdec/src/aacdecoder_lib.cpp
+++ b/libAACdec/src/aacdecoder_lib.cpp
@@ -658,6 +658,8 @@
     goto bail;
   }
   aacDec->hInput = pIn;
+  aacDec->u2wLastFillBytes = -1;
+  aacDec->u2wFillSizeLogged = 0;
 
   aacDec->nrOfLayers = nrOfLayers;
 
@@ -718,6 +720,9 @@
   INT layer      = 0;
   INT nrOfLayers = self->nrOfLayers;
 
+  /* U2W: remember the input byte count; see the output-buffer check in aacDecoder_DecodeFrame. */
+  self->u2wLastFillBytes = (nrOfLayers > 0) ? (INT)bufferSize[0] : -1;
+
   {
     for (layer = 0; layer < nrOfLayers; layer++){
       {
@@ -1052,8 +1057,22 @@
     /* Update Statistics */
     aacDecoder_UpdateBitStreamCounters(&self->streamInfo, hBs, nBits, ErrorStatus);
 
-    /* Check whether external output buffer is large enough. */
-    if (timeDataSize_extern < self->streamInfo.numChannels*self->streamInfo.frameSize) {
+    /* Check whether external output buffer is large enough.
+       U2W: AppleCarPlay's AAC-ELD (call audio) path passes the input byte count it just gave
+       aacDecoder_Fill as timeDataSize (measured in the car 2026-10-19: 2..181, always the
+       packet length, frame 1*480).  That is no output size; fdk-aac 0.1.4, the vendor library,
+       ignored the argument and wrote the frame, and the CarPlay SDK only decodes AAC-ELD into
+       a buffer of at least kAudioSamplesPerPacket_AAC_ELD frames.  Treat exactly that value as
+       "size unknown" and write the frame as 0.1.4 did; every other value is checked. */
+    if (timeDataSize_extern == self->u2wLastFillBytes) {
+      if (!self->u2wFillSizeLogged) {
+        self->u2wFillSizeLogged = 1;
+        FDKprintfErr("fdk-aac: timeDataSize %d is the input byte count, not an output size; "
+                     "writing one frame (%d samples) as fdk-aac 0.1.4 did\n", timeDataSize_extern,
+                     self->streamInfo.numChannels*self->streamInfo.frameSize);
+      }
+    }
+    else if (timeDataSize_extern < self->streamInfo.numChannels*self->streamInfo.frameSize) {
       ErrorStatus = AAC_DEC_OUTPUT_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL;
     }
 
--- a/libAACdec/src/aacdecoder.h
+++ b/libAACdec/src/aacdecoder.h
@@ -227,6 +227,8 @@
   UINT         extGainDelay;                         /*!< Delay that must be accounted for extGain. */
 
   INT_PCM      pcmOutputBuffer[(8)*(2048)];
+  INT          u2wLastFillBytes;   /* U2W: input bytes of the last aacDecoder_Fill (-1: none) */
+  INT          u2wFillSizeLogged;
 
 };
 
